# A site that accepts the connection and doesn't answer left a new tab blank apart from the loading
# bar, and edge to edge or in fullscreen without even that (GitHub #256). Ten seconds without the
# page's first response, the toast says "Still waiting for 127.0.0.1 to respond" with Stop
# Loading; it goes when the page is stopped or answers, and a new wait brings it back. The same in
# a Little Window. ${STALL} accepts connections and never answers one.
# promise: #256
budget rss=800 stalls50=20

cra://open?url=${STALL}/
expect-log page 127\.0\.0\.1 still waiting for a response: notice shown \(navigation 1\)
# ⌘. (Stop Loading) ends the wait: the notice goes with it.
cra://action/stop
expect-log page 127\.0\.0\.1 no longer waiting: notice gone \(navigation 1\)

# Waiting again in the same tab: a new clock, the notice is back.
cra://navigate?url=${STALL}/again
expect-log page 127\.0\.0\.1 still waiting for a response: notice shown \(navigation 2\)
# Another page that answers: gone, and it doesn't come back once that page is loading.
cra://navigate?url=${PAGE}?n=answered
expect-log loaded 127\.0\.0\.1 \(HTTP 200\)
expect-log page 127\.0\.0\.1 no longer waiting: notice gone \(navigation 3\)
wait 1
reject-log notice shown \(navigation 3\)

# A Little Window waiting for the same server.
cra://open?url=${STALL}/little&little=1
expect-log Little Window: page 127\.0\.0\.1 still waiting for a response: notice shown \(navigation 1\)
cra://debug?checkStore=1
